## Visual Design System — "Kalendaryo"

**Normative source: `apps/web/DESIGN.md`.** Read it before any UI work. Summary:

- **World:** the kitchen wall calendar where bills get circled and crossed off. Printed ink (black, calendar red) is what the bank/system says; **ballpen blue** (`primary`) is what the user does.
- **Color tokens:** `background` (paper), `card` (sheet), `muted` (shade), `border` / `input` (rules), `foreground` / `muted-foreground` (ink), `primary` (ballpen), `accent` (ballpen wash), `due` + `due-wash` (calendar red; also `destructive`), `success` + `success-wash` (paid), `warning` + `warning-wash` (SOA missing), `chart-1…8` (categories — no red/green).
- **Type:** one family, Archivo (`--font-sans`). `font-numeral` (condensed heavy tabular) for dates, amounts, counts; `font-headline` for month names and big titles; normal width for everything else. Fixed scale 12/13/14/16/18/22/28/36/48.
- **Shape:** 4px tags, 6px controls, 8px panels; 1px rules; flat surfaces; only `shadow-overlay` for dialogs/sheets/menus/toasts.
- **Building blocks:** `DayMark`, `DateNumeral`, `MonthCalendar` (`components/calendar`), `Amount`, `CardChip`, `Ledger`/`FigureLine`, `StatusBadge`/`BillStatusTag`, `SegmentedControl`, `EmptyState`, `ErrorState` (`components/shared`), skeleton kit (`components/shared/skeletons`).
- **Status grammar:** due = pen circle, due soon/overdue = red circle, paid = check, SOA missing = dashed ring, awaiting SOA = dotted ring, today = filled square. Use `resolveBillState` (`lib/due/bill-state.ts`) so every screen agrees.
- **Never:** gradients, glow, glass, colored side borders, icon-tile stat strips, tracked uppercase eyebrows, raw palette classes (`bg-amber-100`, `text-emerald-600`).

## Responsive Design

### Mobile-First Approach

Always design for mobile first, then enhance for larger screens:

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Mobile-first
<div className="
  grid 
  grid-cols-1         /* Mobile: 1 column */
  sm:grid-cols-2      /* Tablet: 2 columns */
  lg:grid-cols-3      /* Desktop: 3 columns */
  xl:grid-cols-4      /* Large: 4 columns */
  gap-4
">
  {properties.map(property => (
    <PropertyCard key={property.id} property={property} />
  ))}
</div>

// ❌ Bad - Desktop-first (harder to maintain)
<div className="grid grid-cols-4 lg:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-1">
```

